    "title": "Kitchen Operations",
    "notionId": "ab73e516-28c2-8290-b12f-01f437b312e8",
    "category": "Notion OS Module",
    "content": "# Kitchen Operations\r\n\r\nType: `page` | Notion ID: `ab73e516-28c2-8290-b12f-01f437b312e8`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n## Compact UI Navigation\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nKitchen ko ek practical home-system ke roop me organize karna.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Sections\r\n\r\n- Shopping List\r\n- This Week\r\n- All Recipes\r\n- Kitchen Database\r\n- Storage / Pantry Notes\r\n- Cleaning Routine\r\n- Leftovers / Batch Cook\r\n- Tools / Appliances\r\n\r\n## Connected Systems\r\n\r\n- Health & Ayurveda Tracker\r\n- Finance & Investments\r\n- Weekly / Monthly / Annual Reviews\r\n- Knowledge Database\r\n\r\n## Next Step\r\n\r\nIs page ko pantry, recipes, cleaning aur meal-planning views ke saath expand kiya jayega.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Standardization Status\r\n\r\n- Existing content preserved: done\r\n- Pantry / recipes / cleaning / meal-planning expansion: pending\r\n- Database backbone: native pair\r\n- Views: native pair\r\n- Templates: native pair\r\n- Dashboard integration: in progress\r\n\r\n## Next Build\r\n\r\nAdd pantry, recipes, cleaning, and meal-planning views on the native kitchen databases.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Native Kitchen Canon\r\n\r\nThis module now uses the OS-native kitchen pair as the canonical backend:\r\n\r\n- Ingredients (1)\r\n- Recipes (1)\r\n\r\n## Kitchen Dashboard\r\n\r\n- Pantry: ingredient inventory, shopping, and storage\r\n- Recipes: meal planning, favorites, tags, and ingredients\r\n- Cleaning Routine: upkeep and maintenance\r\n- Leftovers / Batch Cook: reuse and prep planning\r\n- Shopping List: low or needed items\r\n\r\n📊 **Database / Collection View: Database** (ID: `4d43e516-28c2-82df-bb76-81a2dc825e32`)\r\n\r\n📊 **Database / Collection View: Database** (ID: `94e3e516-28c2-8243-be87-010cfcb892bf`)\r\n\r\n## Native-Only Summary\r\n\r\n- Canonical backend: Ingredients (1) and Recipes (1)\r\n- Front hub: Kitchen Operations\r\n- Core views: Pantry, Kitchen Recipes\r\n- Working lanes: Shopping List, Cleaning Routine, Leftovers / Batch Cook\r\n- Status: consolidation in progress\r\n\r\n📊 **Database / Collection View: Pantry Purchases (1)** (ID: `94962a2b-f1ca-4616-a8d2-648882e14df3`)\r\n\r\n## Pantry Module\r\n\r\n- **Pantry Inventory:** native Ingredients (1) database, extended for current quantity, reorder point, next purchase quantity, preferred unit, last purchase price/quantity/date, preferred brand and location.\r\n- **Purchase History:** native Pantry Purchases (1) database linked to Ingredients (1), storing purchase date, quantity, unit price, brand, location and calculated total cost.\r\n- **Source import:** uploaded grocery workbook analysed; duplicate copy-sheets were treated as duplicate source material rather than separate inventory items. Source material spans fruits/vegetables and ration/pantry categories.\r\n- **Operational views:** Pantry Inventory and Purchase History.\r\n- **Important boundary:** Notion formula/schema changes can calculate a purchase-line total and store a user-entered next-purchase quantity, but this setup does not automatically derive the next purchase quantity from historical purchase prices without an explicit automation/formula model based on normalized units and price history.\r\n\r\n## Pantry Import Status\r\n\r\n- Existing `Ingredients (1)` records created from the current import batch were moved out of Ingredients and into `Pantry Purchases (1)` so the pre-existing Ingredients records remain unchanged.\r\n- Full source workbook: `Final fruits, sabji, rashan list Jan25-May25.xlsx`\r\n- Source workbook analysis: 580 non-empty cells; 279 normalized unique strings across the workbook; duplicate-copy sheets consolidated rather than treated as separate inventory entities.\r\n- Pantry import uses two operational categories: Fresh Produce and Rashan/Pantry.\r\n- Purchase-source metadata fields added: Import Source, Source Row, Source Category, Duplicate Group.\r\n- Further source-list rows remain to be imported from the workbook; no unverified prices/quantities were invented.\r\n\r\n\r\n## 🗄️ Collections / Databases in this Page\r\n\r\n### Collection: Ingredients (1)\r\nColumns: Day (rollup), Quantity (text), Reorder Point (number), Shopping List (checkbox), Tags (multi_select), Current Qty (number), Purchases (relation), Last Purchase Date (date), Last Purchase Qty (number), Shopping (checkbox), Unit (text), Reorder Status (select), Next Purchase Qty (number), Expiry / Freshness (text), Purchase Notes (text), Created (created_time), Inventory (status), Notes (text), Preferred Brand (text), Preferred Unit (select), Last Purchase Price (number), Category (select), Preferred Location (text), Storage Type (select), Recipes (relation), Ingredients (title)\r\n\r\n### Collection: Recipes (1)\r\nColumns: Created (created_time), Ingredients (relation), Favorites (checkbox), Unit (text), Meal Plan (formula), Prep Time (text), Fav.  (formula), Type (multi_select), Cook Time (text), Notes (text), Day (multi_select), Tag (multi_select), URL (url), Recipes (title)\r\n\r\n### Collection: Pantry Purchases (1)\r\nColumns: Brand (text), Location (text), Total Cost Calc (formula), Import Source (text), Source Category (text), Ingredient (relation), Notes (text), Unit Price (number), Quantity (number), Total Cost (formula), Duplicate Group (text), Purchase Date (date), Source Row (number), Purchase (title), Tags (multi_select), Preferred Unit (select), Next Purchase Qty (number), Purchase Notes (text), Reorder Point (number), Category (select), Current Qty (number)\r\n",
    "byteLength": 5285
