    "content": "# OS Standardization Phase\r\n\r\nType: `page` | Notion ID: `6b03e516-28c2-8377-8183-816a1abdd048`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nCreate one repeatable conversion pattern for every major module in Om Knowledge OS v2.0 so each page can be standardized into: content preservation, properties, relations, views, templates, tags, and sample entries.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Standard Conversion Pattern\r\n\r\n1. Preserve existing real content.\r\n1. Convert major headings into database properties.\r\n1. Convert sub-points under each heading into multi-select options when appropriate.\r\n1. Add relations to related modules.\r\n1. Add tags and content tags.\r\n1. Add sample rows.\r\n1. Add filtered and focused views.\r\n1. Add templates.\r\n1. Surface the module on the dashboard.\r\n\r\n## Recommended Improvement\r\n\r\nUse database-backed hubs for the high-frequency modules first, then connect them through the dashboard:\r\n\r\n- Knowledge Vault\r\n- Ideas Inbox\r\n- Journal & Reflection\r\n- Weekly / Monthly / Annual Reviews\r\n- Research Hub\r\n- Task Intelligence\r\n- Goals (Life Pyramid)\r\n- Universal Inbox\r\n- Reading Library\r\n- Analytics Dashboard\r\n- Health & Ayurveda Tracker\r\n- Astrology & Spiritual Research\r\n- Finance & Investments\r\n- Land & Property Research\r\n- Kitchen Operations\r\n\r\n## Priority Order\r\n\r\n1. Executive Home Dashboard\r\n1. Research Hub\r\n1. Task Intelligence\r\n1. Goals (Life Pyramid)\r\n1. Universal Inbox\r\n1. Reading Library\r\n1. Weekly / Monthly / Annual Reviews\r\n1. Analytics Dashboard\r\n1. Health & Ayurveda Tracker\r\n1. Astrology & Spiritual Research\r\n1. Finance & Investments\r\n1. Land & Property Research\r\n1. Kitchen Operations\r\n\r\n## Module Rule\r\n\r\nEach module should keep the same design language:\r\n\r\n- consistent property naming\r\n- consistent tag taxonomy\r\n- consistent relation strategy\r\n- consistent sample-entry style\r\n- consistent view layout\r\n\r\n## Next Step\r\n\r\nApply this pattern module by module, starting with the dashboard-facing hubs and then the remaining sections.\r\n",
