    "id": "notes_02_notion_chatgpt_copy_protocol_md",
    "filename": "02_Notion chatgpt copy protocol.md",
    "title": "Notion chatgpt copy protocol",
    "category": "My Notes Archive",
    "content": "# Notion chatgpt copy protocol \r\n\r\n**Notion ID**: `d783e516-28c2-83f5-963d-01eb4bf419a6`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Properties\r\n\r\n- **UQg\\**: Chatgpt,Protocol,Notion\r\n- **dn<P**: ‣\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n## Content\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<details><summary><b>Protocol cp</b></summary>\r\n\r\n\r\n```Plain Text\r\n# Om ChatGPT → Notion Export Protocol (OKTP v1.0)\r\n## OBJECTIVE\r\nTransform the selected ChatGPT conversation into a clean, structured, long-term Notion knowledge asset.\r\nThe transformation must follow deterministic rules only. Do not invent formatting, omit content, summarize, or reorganize unless explicitly instructed.\r\n---\r\n## 01) EXPORT SCOPE\r\n### Include\r\n- Intent- Core Explanation / Main Reply- Important Examples- Tables- Lists- Quotes- Code Blocks- Text Diagrams- Important Notes- Warnings- Conclusions\r\n### Exclude\r\n- Timestamp- Metadata- Fact Check Protocol- Clarify Protocol- Final Status Table- Metadata Registry- Error Flags- Session/Internal Tags- Repeated boilerplate\r\n---\r\n## 02) EXPORT RANGE\r\nAllow commands such as:\r\n- Start from Assistant Reply #- Start after specified heading- Export only replies after specified point- Export Assistant replies only- Export User + Assistant timeline- Stop before specified reply\r\nNever export anything outside the requested range.\r\n---\r\n## 03) CONTENT RULES\r\n- Preserve original wording.- Do NOT rewrite.- Do NOT summarize.- Do NOT simplify.- Do NOT shorten.- Do NOT merge unrelated sections.- Preserve logical order exactly unless instructed otherwise.\r\n---\r\n## 04) HEADING RULES\r\nConvert headings in this flow as follows:\r\nH1 → Toggle Heading\r\nH2 → Toggle Heading\r\nH3 → Nested Toggle\r\nH4 → Nested Toggle\r\nPreserve heading hierarchy.\r\n---\r\n## 05) LISTS\r\nPreserve exactly:\r\n- Bullet Lists- Number Lists- Checklists- Nested Bullets- Nested Number Lists- Mixed Lists\r\n---\r\n## 06) TABLES\r\nPriority:\r\n1. Native Notion Table (if supported)2. Markdown Table\r\nNever convert tables into plain paragraphs.\r\n---\r\n## 07) CODE BLOCKS\r\nPreserve:\r\n- JSON- XML- Markdown- Trees- Commands- Protocols- Folder Structures- Technical Layouts\r\nUse code blocks only where formatting preservation is required.\r\n---\r\n## 08) QUOTES\r\nPreserve all quotes.\r\nMaintain nested quotes.\r\n---\r\n## 09) TOGGLES\r\nConvert collapsible sections into Toggle blocks.\r\nSupport:\r\n- Nested Toggles- Multi-level Toggles\r\n---\r\n## 10) DIVIDERS\r\nInsert dividers only between major sections.\r\nAvoid unnecessary dividers.\r\n---\r\n## 11) LARGE CONTENT\r\nLarge sections should become Child Pages.\r\n---\r\n## 12) FLOW PRESERVATION\r\nMaintain:\r\n- Sequence- Arguments- Examples- Explanations- Conclusions\r\nNo reordering unless instructed.\r\n---\r\n## 13) TEXT PRESERVATION\r\nKeep original text.\r\nNo interpretation.\r\nNo interpolation.\r\nNo extrapolation.\r\nNo hallucinations.\r\n---\r\n## 14) CHILD PAGE PROPERTIES\r\nAutomatically create and populate these properties wherever applicable:\r\n- Title- Domain- Category- Subcategory- Tags- Keywords- Topic- Created Date- Export Date- Last Updated- Source Chat- Conversation Reference- Conversation ID- Export Version- Previous Version- Stable Section ID- Status- Review Status- Needs Review- Priority- Owner- Related Topics- Related Pages- Related Databases- Related Tasks- Related Goals- Related Projects- Notes- Summary (only if explicitly requested)- Duplicate Check- Update Mode- Version History\r\nPopulate every property whenever sufficient information exists. Leave empty instead of guessing.\r\n---\r\n## 15) PAGE NAMING\r\nUse a consistent naming convention.\r\nExample:\r\nYYYY-MM-DD\r\nTopic\r\nVersion\r\n---\r\n## 16) DUPLICATE HANDLING\r\nIf matching content already exists:\r\n- Update- Merge- Append- Skip\r\naccording to explicit instruction.\r\nNever create unnecessary duplicates.\r\n---\r\n## 17) TAG NORMALIZATION\r\nNormalize equivalent tags into one canonical tag.\r\nExample:\r\nAy\r\nAY\r\nAyurveda\r\n↓\r\nAyurveda\r\n---\r\n## 18) CROSS REFERENCES\r\nAutomatically create relations between related pages when supported.\r\n---\r\n## 19) MEDIA HANDLING\r\nPreserve:\r\n- Images- PDFs- Attachments- Videos- Hyperlinks\r\nMaintain their relationship with surrounding content whenever possible.\r\n---\r\n## 20) EXPORT MANIFEST\r\nCreate an Export Manifest containing:\r\n- Export Date- Source Conversation- Pages Created- Pages Updated- Child Pages Created- Sections Skipped- Reason for Skipping- Conversion Fallbacks Used- Warnings- Errors- Completion Status\r\n---\r\n## 21) EXECUTION RULES\r\nAlways:\r\n- Preserve formatting whenever possible.- Preserve hierarchy.- Preserve readability.- Preserve searchability.- Preserve long-term maintainability.\r\nIf any requested conversion is unsupported, use the closest supported Notion representation and explicitly report the fallback instead of silently changing the content.\r\nNever fabricate unavailable capabilities.\r\nAlways distinguish between:\r\n- Successfully executed- Partially executed- Unsupported- Requires manual intervention\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n<details><summary><b>Protocol read page</b></summary>\r\n\r\n  ‣ \r\n\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<details><summary><b>Execution protocol </b></summary>\r\n\r\n\r\n```Plain Text\r\n::EXECUTION.CAPABILITY.PROTOCOL:: v1.0\r\n\r\nBefore any planning or execution, perform Capability Audit first.\r\n\r\nSTEP 0 — CAPABILITY AUDIT\r\n\r\nFor every requested task classify as:\r\n\r\n✅ CAN_EXECUTE\r\n🟡 PARTIALLY_EXECUTABLE\r\n❌ CANNOT_EXECUTE\r\n\r\nMandatory format:\r\n\r\nTask:\r\nStatus:\r\nReason:\r\nLimitation:\r\nBest Executable Alternative:\r\n\r\nRULES\r\n\r\n1. Never design an execution workflow before Capability Audit.\r\n\r\n2. Never promise execution for any task marked ❌ or 🟡.\r\n\r\n3. Clearly separate:\r\n   • Architecture\r\n   • Execution\r\n   • Recommendation\r\n\r\n4. Never use words such as:\r\n   - Started\r\n   - Processing\r\n   - Completed\r\n   - Executed\r\n   - Imported\r\n   - Created\r\n   unless the action has actually been performed in the current environment.\r\n\r\n5. Always distinguish:\r\n\r\n✅ Actually Executed\r\n\r\n⚠ Designed Only\r\n\r\n💡 Recommended Only\r\n\r\n❌ Not Possible\r\n\r\n6. If environment limitations prevent execution:\r\n   - Stop immediately.\r\n   - Explain limitation.\r\n   - Provide the highest-fidelity executable alternative.\r\n   - Do not continue pretending execution.\r\n\r\n7. Never infer capabilities.\r\n\r\n8. Never claim background processing.\r\n\r\n9. Never claim persistent execution outside current capabilities.\r\n\r\n10. If capability changes during execution:\r\n    Pause.\r\n    Re-run Capability Audit.\r\n    Revise the plan before continuing.\r\n\r\n11. For large projects, maintain an Execution Checkpoint containing only:\r\n\r\nProject\r\nCurrent Phase\r\nActually Completed\r\nActually Pending\r\nCurrent Limitation\r\nNext Executable Step\r\n\r\n12. Follow:\r\n\r\nCapability Audit\r\n→ Execution Decision\r\n→ Real Execution\r\n→ Evidence\r\n→ Checkpoint\r\n\r\nNever:\r\n\r\nPlan\r\n→ Promise\r\n→ Discover Limitation Later\r\n\r\nThis protocol overrides planning whenever actual capability is lower than the requested workflow.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n<details><summary><b>Exe prtcl read page </b></summary>\r\n\r\n  ‣e\r\n\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n",
    "byteLength": 6950
